<in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock contextRef="OneD">Above reviewed by Audit Comm its meeting and approved by Board  in meeting held on 14.08.2023. The auditors have conducted limited review of financial results and have expressed an unmodified opinion 2.Co. has investment amounting to  5,103.34 lakhs in Indian Furniture Products Limited (IFPL), a subsidiary company which is in buss of distribution &amp; retailing furniture &amp; related item. On review of current situation and future prospects of furniture business, the Co. recognised impairment loss on investment for the yr ended 31.03.2023 amounting to  591.64 lakhs. 3. Sugar buss of Company seasonal in nature wherein sugar cane crushing  takes place b/w November to May, while sales takes place throughout the year. Performance of Co. varies. 4.  The Board , via resolution 13.02.2023 accorded  consent Scheme of Amalgamation between the Co. and Zuari Sugar &amp; Power Limited (ZSPL) (a WOS of Co.) &amp; respective shareholders and creditors (‘the Scheme’). The Board of ZSPL accorded consent to the Scheme resolution 31.01.23. The appointed date of Amalgamation as per the Scheme is 01.04.22. Pursuant to first hearing application  on 11.05 23, NCLT dispensed with the holding of meetings of shareholders and creditors of ZIL. Pursuant to second motion application filed on 23.06.23, the final hearing will be on 14.09.23. 5) Notes relating to Unaudited consolidated financial results of Zuari Infraworld India Limited (ZIIL) (a Subsidiary of ZIL) for the quarter ended 30.06.23:  a)ZIIL made advance payment aggregated to INR 639.61 lakhs under Development Mgmt Agreement to agencies which entitled to certain % of income calculated in the manner specified, which will adjusted in yr when the agency becomes entitled to share of income as per agreement. One of the operating creditors of one of the Agency co. initiated corporate insolvency resolution process against that Co. The Co. mgmt initiated legal proceedings for recovery &amp;  Co. mgmt doesn't expect significant effect on balance and expects to recover same in full, accordingly no adjustment is considered necessary b)Recoverable advances as at 30.06.23 paid in 2017 to a sub-contractor aggregates to 2,246.49 lakhs including interest accrued 33.72 lakhs. The Co. mgmt currently initiated legal proceeding  &amp; optimistic to recover.Hence in the view of the Mgmt, no provision  considered necessary at this stage. c) Zuari Infra Middle East Limited, UAE (a wholly owned foreign subsidiary), in Interim Condensed consolidated financial information, has taken provision for impairment of AED 22.95 million, and transferred AED 158.62 million, as promoter contribution, to Burj District One Limited (50% joint venture company), which owns a plot of land on which project “Exquisite Living Residencies” is developed .8 Notes relating to unaudited consolidated financial results of Zuari Agro Chemicals Limited (ZACL) (an Associate of ZIL) quarter ended 30.06.23:  a)Mangalore Chemicals &amp; Fertilizers Limited (MCFL), subsidairy of ZACL, during yr ended 31.03.21 recognized urea subsidy income of  29.14 crores without benchmarking cost of production using naphtha with that of gas-based urea manufacturing units recently converted to natural gas, as notified by the Department of Fertilizers (DoF) for subsidy income computation, against which MCFL has filed writ petition against the DoF before the Hon’ble High Court of Delhi (DHC). Pending finalization of writ petition before the DHC, Co mgmt of subsidiary, based on legal opinion &amp; considering fact that energy cost alwayspass through in subsidy computation, believes artificial benchmarking arbitrary &amp; confident of realization of aforesaid income. b)The Board  of Adventz Trading DMCC (ATD), a foreign subsidiary of ZACL, on 31.03. 23 approved liquidation of operation, subject to approval of RBI and other Authorities. ATD  changed basis of preparing financial statement from going concern to liquidation basis. Hence it has not considered for Consolidation</in-bse-fin:DisclosureOfNotesOnFinancialResultsExplanatoryTextBlock>
